{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "cf93a976-8bff-52e3-b0be-dfafe4588835",
    "name": "EdisonUPM - Sprint 1",
    "description": "REST API of the EdisonUPM backend (Spring Boot, branch main).\n\n**Identity (temporary):** there is no login yet. Requests that need a user send the header `X-User-Id` with a user UUID from `database/02_seed.sql`. No header = anonymous visitor.\n\n**Folder A** is the Sprint 1 smoke test (8 requests with automated checks). **Folder B** documents every other endpoint.\n\n**Status codes:** 200/201/204 success; 400 malformed JSON or invalid value; 401 missing or unknown X-User-Id; 403 not allowed (wrong role or not the owner); 404 not found or not visible; 413 file over 5 MB; 422 validation error with `errors` grouped by field or wizard step.\n\nSee `postman/README.md`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "A - Sprint 1 Smoke Test",
      "description": "Run these 8 requests **in order** (Collection Runner, this folder only). Each request saves the ids it creates into the selected environment, so the next one can use them.\n\nRequest 1 resets `ideaId`, `attachmentId`, `commentId` and creates a new `runTag`, so the folder can be rerun as often as you like.\n\nRequest 3 uploads `fixtures/edison-smoke-test.png`. If Postman cannot find it, open request 3, go to **Body → form-data → file** and select any small PNG image.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. Create idea draft",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-User-Id",
                "value": "{{founderId}}",
                "type": "text",
                "description": "Temporary identity header: the UUID of the acting user (see database/02_seed.sql)."
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/ideas",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "ideas"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Wizard step 1 (Basics). Only users with role STUDENT can create ideas. The idea starts as DRAFT.\n\nSaves `ideaId`.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"title\": \"Smoke test idea {{runTag}}\",\n  \"elevatorPitch\": \"A quick idea created by the Sprint 1 Postman smoke test.\",\n  \"problemStatement\": \"The team needs a repeatable way to check the Sprint 1 workflow.\",\n  \"solutionDescription\": \"Run the eight smoke-test requests in order against a disposable database.\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Fresh values for every run, so the smoke test can be rerun on the same database.",
                  "pm.environment.set('runTag', 'SMOKE-' + Date.now());",
                  "['ideaId', 'attachmentId', 'attachmentUrl', 'attachmentSize', 'commentId', 'clientRequestId']",
                  "    .forEach(key => pm.environment.set(key, ''));"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const UUID = /^[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}$/i;",
                  "pm.test('Environment \"EdisonUPM Local\" is selected', () => pm.expect(pm.environment.name, 'select the EdisonUPM Local environment').to.be.ok);",
                  "pm.test('Status is 201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const idea = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Response has the required idea fields', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(idea).to.include.all.keys('id', 'title', 'elevatorPitch', 'problemStatement', 'solutionDescription', 'status', 'founder', 'screenshots', 'createdAt');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Idea id is a UUID', () => pm.expect(idea.id).to.match(UUID));",
                  "pm.test('New idea is a DRAFT', () => pm.expect(idea.status).to.eql('DRAFT'));",
                  "pm.test('Title was saved', () => pm.expect(idea.title).to.eql('Smoke test idea ' + pm.environment.get('runTag')));",
                  "pm.test('Founder is the founderId user', () => pm.expect(idea.founder.id).to.eql(pm.variables.get('founderId')));",
                  "if (idea.id) { pm.environment.set('ideaId', idea.id); }"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Set tags and development stage",
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-User-Id",
                "value": "{{founderId}}",
                "type": "text",
                "description": "Temporary identity header: the UUID of the acting user (see database/02_seed.sql)."
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/ideas/{{ideaId}}/classification",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "ideas",
                "{{ideaId}}",
                "classification"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Wizard step 2. `tags`: 1 to 3 values from GET /api/tags. `developmentStage`: one value from GET /api/development-stages.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"tags\": [\n    \"SOFTWARE\",\n    \"ED_TECH\"\n  ],\n  \"developmentStage\": \"PROTOTYPE\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const idea = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Same idea was updated', () => pm.expect(idea.id).to.eql(pm.environment.get('ideaId')));",
                  "pm.test('Tags were saved', () => pm.expect(idea.tags).to.have.members(['SOFTWARE', 'ED_TECH']));",
                  "pm.test('Development stage was saved', () => pm.expect(idea.developmentStage).to.eql('PROTOTYPE'));",
                  "pm.test('Idea is still a DRAFT', () => pm.expect(idea.status).to.eql('DRAFT'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "3. Upload screenshot",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-User-Id",
                "value": "{{founderId}}",
                "type": "text",
                "description": "Temporary identity header: the UUID of the acting user (see database/02_seed.sql)."
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/ideas/{{ideaId}}/attachments",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "ideas",
                "{{ideaId}}",
                "attachments"
              ]
            },
            "description": "multipart/form-data with one field named `file`. PNG, JPG or WebP, max 5 MB, max 5 per idea, draft ideas only. Postman sets the Content-Type header automatically.\n\nSaves `attachmentId`.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "file",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": "fixtures/edison-smoke-test.png",
                  "description": "Select a small PNG image if this path is not found."
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const UUID = /^[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}$/i;",
                  "pm.test('Status is 201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const a = pm.response.json();",
                  "const ideaId = pm.environment.get('ideaId');",
                  "pm.test('Response has the required attachment fields', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(a).to.include.all.keys('id', 'fileName', 'contentType', 'sizeBytes', 'displayOrder', 'url', 'uploadedAt');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Attachment id is a UUID', () => pm.expect(a.id).to.match(UUID));",
                  "pm.test('Stored as a PNG image', () => pm.expect(a.contentType).to.eql('image/png'));",
                  "pm.test('File is not empty', () => pm.expect(a.sizeBytes).to.be.above(0));",
                  "pm.test('First screenshot of the idea', () => pm.expect(a.displayOrder).to.eql(0));",
                  "pm.test('Download URL belongs to this idea', () => pm.expect(a.url).to.eql('/api/ideas/' + ideaId + '/attachments/' + a.id + '/file'));",
                  "if (a.id) {",
                  "    pm.environment.set('attachmentId', a.id);",
                  "    pm.environment.set('attachmentUrl', a.url);",
                  "    pm.environment.set('attachmentSize', String(a.sizeBytes));",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "4. Publish idea",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-User-Id",
                "value": "{{founderId}}",
                "type": "text",
                "description": "Temporary identity header: the UUID of the acting user (see database/02_seed.sql)."
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/ideas/{{ideaId}}/publish",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "ideas",
                "{{ideaId}}",
                "publish"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Wizard step 3. Checks every step again; on failure returns 422 with errors grouped as `basics`, `mvpProof` and `review`.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"feedbackEnabled\": true,\n  \"allowedCommenterRoles\": [\n    \"STUDENT\",\n    \"PROFESSOR\"\n  ],\n  \"visibility\": \"PUBLIC\",\n  \"declarationAccepted\": true\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const idea = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Same idea was published', () => pm.expect(idea.id).to.eql(pm.environment.get('ideaId')));",
                  "pm.test('Status is PUBLISHED', () => pm.expect(idea.status).to.eql('PUBLISHED'));",
                  "pm.test('publishedAt is set', () => pm.expect(idea.publishedAt).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty);",
                  "pm.test('Visibility is PUBLIC', () => pm.expect(idea.visibility).to.eql('PUBLIC'));",
                  "pm.test('Students may comment', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(idea.feedbackEnabled).to.eql(true);",
                  "    pm.expect(idea.allowedCommenterRoles).to.include('STUDENT');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Uploaded screenshot is attached', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(idea.screenshots.map(s => s.id)).to.include(pm.environment.get('attachmentId'));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "5. Browse published ideas",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/ideas?q={{runTag}}&size=50",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "ideas"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "q",
                  "value": "{{runTag}}"
                },
                {
                  "key": "size",
                  "value": "50"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Sent without X-User-Id, like a visitor who is not logged in: only PUBLIC ideas are returned. `q` filters by this run's tag so the new idea is always on the first page."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const page = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Response is a page of ideas', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(page).to.include.all.keys('content', 'page', 'size', 'totalElements', 'totalPages');",
                  "    pm.expect(page.content).to.be.an('array');",
                  "});",
                  "const found = page.content.find(i => i.id === pm.environment.get('ideaId'));",
                  "pm.test('Published idea appears in the public list', () => pm.expect(found, 'idea not found in GET /api/ideas').to.exist);",
                  "pm.test('Listed idea is PUBLISHED with its tags and stage', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(found.status).to.eql('PUBLISHED');",
                  "    pm.expect(found.tags).to.have.members(['SOFTWARE', 'ED_TECH']);",
                  "    pm.expect(found.developmentStage).to.eql('PROTOTYPE');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "6. Download screenshot",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/ideas/{{ideaId}}/attachments/{{attachmentId}}/file",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "ideas",
                "{{ideaId}}",
                "attachments",
                "{{attachmentId}}",
                "file"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Returns the image bytes. Postman shows the picture in the response panel."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Content-Type is image/png', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Content-Type')).to.include('image/png'));",
                  "pm.test('Browser MIME sniffing is disabled', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('X-Content-Type-Options')).to.eql('nosniff'));",
                  "const bytes = pm.response.stream;",
                  "pm.test('Body is a real PNG file', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(bytes.length).to.be.above(8);",
                  "    pm.expect([bytes[0], bytes[1], bytes[2], bytes[3]]).to.eql([0x89, 0x50, 0x4E, 0x47]);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Same size as the uploaded file', () => pm.expect(bytes.length).to.eql(Number(pm.environment.get('attachmentSize'))));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "7. Create comment",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-User-Id",
                "value": "{{commenterId}}",
                "type": "text",
                "description": "Temporary identity header: the UUID of the acting user (see database/02_seed.sql)."
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/ideas/{{ideaId}}/comments",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "ideas",
                "{{ideaId}}",
                "comments"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Posted by a different student (`commenterId`). `clientRequestId` is optional: resending the same value returns the comment already created instead of a duplicate. The pre-request script generates a new one each run.\n\nSaves `commentId`.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"content\": \"Smoke test comment for {{runTag}} - looks promising\",\n  \"clientRequestId\": \"{{clientRequestId}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// A new clientRequestId on every run, so the API never returns an older comment.",
                  "pm.environment.set('clientRequestId', pm.variables.replaceIn('{{$guid}}'));"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const UUID = /^[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}$/i;",
                  "pm.test('Status is 201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const c = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Response has the required comment fields', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(c).to.include.all.keys('id', 'ideaId', 'author', 'content', 'createdAt');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Comment id is a UUID', () => pm.expect(c.id).to.match(UUID));",
                  "pm.test('Comment belongs to the idea', () => pm.expect(c.ideaId).to.eql(pm.environment.get('ideaId')));",
                  "pm.test('Author is the commenterId user', () => pm.expect(c.author.id).to.eql(pm.variables.get('commenterId')));",
                  "pm.test('Content was saved', () => pm.expect(c.content).to.eql('Smoke test comment for ' + pm.environment.get('runTag') + ' - looks promising'));",
                  "if (c.id) { pm.environment.set('commentId', c.id); }"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "8. List comments",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/ideas/{{ideaId}}/comments",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "ideas",
                "{{ideaId}}",
                "comments"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Visible comments, newest first, plus `count`. Sent without X-User-Id (public idea)."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Response has count and comments', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(body.count).to.be.a('number');",
                  "    pm.expect(body.comments).to.be.an('array');",
                  "    pm.expect(body.count).to.eql(body.comments.length);",
                  "});",
                  "const c = body.comments.find(x => x.id === pm.environment.get('commentId'));",
                  "pm.test('New comment is listed', () => pm.expect(c, 'comment not found').to.exist);",
                  "pm.test('Listed comment is linked to the idea and the commenter', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(c.ideaId).to.eql(pm.environment.get('ideaId'));",
                  "    pm.expect(c.author.id).to.eql(pm.variables.get('commenterId'));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "B - Complete API Reference",
      "description": "Every other endpoint implemented in the controllers (`backend/src/main/java/es/upm/edison/controller`). These requests have no automated tests; they document the request format and the responses the code can return. They use the ids saved by folder A. Some of them change data (archive, delete): use a disposable database.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Reference data",
          "description": "Fixed lists used by the publication wizard.",
          "item": [
            {
              "name": "List tags",
              "request": {
                "method": "GET",
                "header": [],
                "url": {
                  "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/tags",
                  "host": [
                    "{{baseUrl}}"
                  ],
                  "path": [
                    "api",
                    "tags"
                  ]
                },
                "description": "All idea tags (enum IdeaTag).\n\n**Possible responses**\n- 200 `[\"GREEN_TECH\", \"SOFTWARE\", ...]`\n\nErrors use the body `{timestamp, status, message, errors}`."
              },
              "response": []
            },
            {
              "name": "List development stages",
              "request": {
                "method": "GET",
                "header": [],
                "url": {
                  "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/development-stages",
                  "host": [
                    "{{baseUrl}}"
                  ],
                  "path": [
                    "api",
                    "development-stages"
                  ]
                },
                "description": "All stages (enum DevelopmentStage).\n\n**Possible responses**\n- 200 `[\"CONCEPT\", \"PROTOTYPE\", \"MVP_LIVE\"]`\n\nErrors use the body `{timestamp, status, message, errors}`."
              },
              "response": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Ideas",
          "description": "IdeaController + IdeaService.",
          "item": [
            {
              "name": "Browse ideas with filters",
              "request": {
                "method": "GET",
                "header": [
                  {
                    "key": "X-User-Id",
                    "value": "{{founderId}}",
                    "type": "text",
                    "description": "Temporary identity header: the UUID of the acting user (see database/02_seed.sql).",
                    "disabled": true
                  }
                ],
                "url": {
                  "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/ideas?q=campus&tag=SOFTWARE&page=0&size=12",
                  "host": [
                    "{{baseUrl}}"
                  ],
                  "path": [
                    "api",
                    "ideas"
                  ],
                  "query": [
                    {
                      "key": "q",
                      "value": "campus",
                      "description": "Text in title or elevator pitch"
                    },
                    {
                      "key": "tag",
                      "value": "SOFTWARE",
                      "description": "One tag from GET /api/tags"
                    },
                    {
                      "key": "page",
                      "value": "0"
                    },
                    {
                      "key": "size",
                      "value": "12"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                "description": "Same endpoint as smoke request 5, showing every filter. Anonymous users see PUBLIC ideas; STUDENT and PROFESSOR users (X-User-Id) also see UPM_COMMUNITY ideas. Sorted by publishedAt, newest first. `page` starts at 0; `size` 1-50 (default 12).\n\n**Possible responses**\n- 200 page `{content: [IdeaSummary], page, size, totalElements, totalPages}`\n- 400 unknown `tag` value\n\nErrors use the body `{timestamp, status, message, errors}`."
              },
              "response": []
            },
            {
              "name": "My ideas",
              "request": {
                "method": "GET",
                "header": [
                  {
                    "key": "X-User-Id",
                    "value": "{{founderId}}",
                    "type": "text",
                    "description": "Temporary identity header: the UUID of the acting user (see database/02_seed.sql)."
                  }
                ],
                "url": {
                  "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/ideas/mine",
                  "host": [
                    "{{baseUrl}}"
                  ],
                  "path": [
                    "api",
                    "ideas",
                    "mine"
                  ]
                },
                "description": "All ideas of the current user, any status, newest first.\n\n**Possible responses**\n- 200 `[IdeaSummary]`\n- 401 missing or unknown X-User-Id\n\nErrors use the body `{timestamp, status, message, errors}`."
              },
              "response": []
            },
            {
              "name": "Idea details",
              "request": {
                "method": "GET",
                "header": [
                  {
                    "key": "X-User-Id",
                    "value": "{{founderId}}",
                    "type": "text",
                    "description": "Temporary identity header: the UUID of the acting user (see database/02_seed.sql)."
                  }
                ],
                "url": {
                  "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/ideas/{{ideaId}}",
                  "host": [
                    "{{baseUrl}}"
                  ],
                  "path": [
                    "api",
                    "ideas",
                    "{{ideaId}}"
                  ]
                },
                "description": "Full idea including screenshots. Founders also see their own drafts.\n\n**Possible responses**\n- 200 Idea\n- 401 UPM_COMMUNITY idea requested without X-User-Id\n- 404 idea does not exist or is not visible to this user\n- 400 id is not a UUID\n\nErrors use the body `{timestamp, status, message, errors}`."
              },
              "response": []
            },
            {
              "name": "Edit basics (draft)",
              "request": {
                "method": "PUT",
                "header": [
                  {
                    "key": "X-User-Id",
                    "value": "{{founderId}}",
